// ═══ CAUSE 1: Slow IO without timeout ═══
// Each request: new thread → httpClient.send(request) → NO TIMEOUT!
// HTTP server down → TCP timeout = 300 seconds!
// 100 requests/sec × 300 sec wait = 30,000 threads after 5 minutes!
// All threads: TIMED_WAITING in SocketInputStream.read()
// CPU: 0% (nobody computing, all waiting for network!)
// FIX: httpClient.connectTimeout(5s).readTimeout(5s)

// ═══ CAUSE 2: Thread leak ═══
void handleRequest(Request req) {
    new Thread(() -> processAsync(req)).start();  // NEW thread per request!
    // Thread finishes but: if processAsync hangs → thread never terminates!
    // Or: Executors.newCachedThreadPool() → creates thread per task!
    // Count: only grows! Never shrinks (no shutdown, no timeout)!
}
// FIX: bounded ThreadPoolExecutor! Reuse threads! shutdown()!

// ═══ CAUSE 3: Connection pool exhausted ═══
// HikariCP maxPoolSize = 10. Each query takes 2 seconds (slow query!).
// 10 connections in use → thread 11: WAITING in HikariPool.getConnection()
// 100 concurrent requests → 90 threads WAITING → count rises!
// CPU: 0% (threads waiting for connections, not computing!)
// FIX: increase pool + optimize slow query + add timeout on getConnection()

// ═══ INVESTIGATION: jstack ═══
// jstack <PID> > dump.txt
// grep -c "BLOCKED\|WAITING\|TIMED_WAITING" dump.txt → count idle threads!
// grep "SocketInputStream.read" dump.txt → slow HTTP calls!
// grep "HikariPool.getConnection" dump.txt → DB pool exhausted!
// grep "Thread.sleep\|Object.wait" dump.txt → waiting on locks/conditions!
// Watch thread count: jcmd <PID> Thread.print | grep "Thread-" | wc -l

// ═══ WHY "ADD MORE THREADS/SERVERS" IS WRONG ═══
// More threads → more threads WAITING on same slow dependency!
// 200 threads waiting on slow DB → increase to 400 → 400 threads waiting!
// More servers → more connections to same DB → DB overloaded → even slower!
// Fix the ROOT CAUSE: timeout, fix slow query, cache, circuit breaker!
